{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/build.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:24:31.784391Z","id":"7a96ebb5ba932b732f23b33736801444b64544c02261b89bafd8ba593ec05bae","body":{"detail":"lane_worker in scripts/quality_gates.sh runs crates/clax-worker/test-wasm.mjs, which runs build.sh: off macOS it uses clang and the newest llvm-ar* on PATH, and on its first run cargo installs worker-build 0.8.7 into target/tools (minutes, cold). .github/workflows/ci.yml:13 and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target. Whether ubuntu-latest's clang targets wasm32 and has an llvm-ar, and how long the lane takes cold there, was not checked; the first CI run shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"041427a2c0539298d3df3b7ce38d3930263f6d5702d96afa69c26ad1e5cf1d5b"},"summary":"The worker lane's wasm build has run only on macOS: CI's Ubuntu runner and build.sh's Linux branch are unverified","tags":["gates","ci","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819630Z","id":"93f1c8f7fcce808be359bfa4edee23928f3fbeab6bb9e2d764001a0b0f0b420a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"3009a302208a3d2a63dba6e2cdbc23240a6e50a624d65c65da64b7be7cfbf5eb"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-clone.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:16:47.746409Z","id":"9490f5aaa9b490a578907887ffe222d66d8a93de6e5067baa854cdca51cb820c","body":{"detail":"On the Worker every browser is a LAN viewer (record df3fe77c on crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs, hosted: None), so no browser reaches the git token routes as a person. The check sends Authorization: Bearer <CLAX_TOKEN> with every request, frame content included, and with it the page shows 'Comment mode could not load in this page' (the bridge on the artifact origin); the Clone checks do not depend on it. Once the Worker serves signed-in members (hosted mode), the check should sign a member in instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"8e3a4b0a50d6a53ed34fdedc3586ea9aef33f7e961dc8c72915045e868eacb08"},"summary":"The Clone dialog's Worker check signs the browser in by sending the owner token on every request: the Worker has no owner browser yet","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:27:26.058068Z","id":"af73cb2ed383f881021b778eb2194604afc102070e02a2aec2299aed7bb0c6b6","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own workspace and uses clax-core, clax-rt and clax-server by path; its Cargo.lock was extended from the spike's, not seeded from the root Cargo.lock. A dependency the root pins (axum 0.8.9, rusqlite 0.40.2 agree today) can drift. Joining the root workspace would share one lockfile but pull workers-rs into every native build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"b4c283574e347d9e3c895617432c5fd93a908f1f9277cc5f7cce8804ba4aca1d"},"summary":"The Worker's lockfile resolves the Clax crates' dependencies apart from the root's, so the Worker may build them at other versions than the daemon","supersedes":"93f1c8f7fcce808be359bfa4edee23928f3fbeab6bb9e2d764001a0b0f0b420a","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-clone.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T11:58:17.360120Z","id":"21c1bcecc8c950072d2ce2c4ca94f3a4c2e8d5ab3a22e224e3e8220feb0e3a0f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5be6ea74","summary":"Fixed: the check runs the Worker hosted and signs Ada in with the setup secret, her browser carrying only its session cookie; npm run e2e:clone passes every check, including 'the page shows no comment-mode failure' at 1280 and 390, light and dark, and Sam offered read alone.","supersedes":"9490f5aaa9b490a578907887ffe222d66d8a93de6e5067baa854cdca51cb820c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/e2e-publish.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:13:10.748920Z","id":"e7e61e071d45155206aa092dc95df07d7f20eb8b84162af3b2867e2c9de80a56","body":{"detail":"Like e2e-hosted.mjs, it runs only by hand (npm run e2e:publish with CLAX_TEST_BIN set), since it needs a clax binary beside the Worker build. The native path is covered in the gates by crates/clax-server/tests/api_remotes.rs and crates/clax-cli/tests/remote_push.rs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"75d8bcda59fdd9cffe6a5608889f53cf63c50ffac07fc242b1547da2433a1784"},"summary":"The Worker's publish e2e is not run by scripts/quality_gates.sh","tags":["testing","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231877Z","id":"514d6135284b54f9bfaa4bcf914f69f84183228301ae0a447aeb5f3154b2d840","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"3f94c1ef605bbf4f9236d3a3617324915d8794ac3882a04c08cb89544e148941"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.231915Z","id":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":276},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:34:23.232163Z","id":"4854d787a4833aea89d19dd5e75c7a3143dfe78c2612be02169652b1731c3277","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":588},"content_hash":"765d646f83c57f6bfd8c11ce9c56e0694989cbb0bd8310228dc0a9cf9e38cdfc"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:04:35.038836Z","id":"1cdb4d61ee59652c4354b89553a4e030696e48a5382d37f7e827c80cdab0cfad","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","summary":"Checked: writeRecord writes the record with mode 0o600 and chmods it 0600 again, and crates/clax-worker/.gitignore lists .deploy/. Plain-text storage itself is unchanged; left open for the owner.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:46:48.117278Z","id":"a3e8251c3f14d646150e8c2a8d326dd42aa53683c1de7647a870e7959b5737cc","body":{"detail":"Run in sequence after the other Worker e2e lanes; two later runs alone passed. The Worker answers the oversized body before reading it (the body caps), which wrangler dev's proxy sometimes turns into a lost connection. The e2e-hosted lane follows its chunked oversized bodies with a request that may fail for the same reason.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":584},"end":{"line":585},"content_hash":"df0793a0b2b4eb9b97ad52f463593d700501072fbce6616032fdcc9bf4fc1e85"},"summary":"The 13 MiB push check failed once in three runs: git saw HTTP 500 where 413 was expected, wrangler logging 'Network connection lost' for the receive-pack POST","tags":["worker","test","flake","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"61c8252ad530041c277dd059809fb9481703393efcc1eced47a4d98523f42ed2","body":{"detail":"Only the logged-out --dry-run ran (no account was available): node deploy.mjs --dry-run --zone example.com passes and ends at wrangler deploy --dry-run (11.36 MiB, 4.36 MiB gzipped). Each logged-in step throws with wrangler's last error line and the command it ran, so a wrong pattern shows as a failed step rather than silently. If namespaces list answers a shape jsonIn does not parse, the namespace is taken as missing and a probe repository is created and deleted, which is harmless.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":234},"content_hash":"3f94c1ef605bbf4f9236d3a3617324915d8794ac3882a04c08cb89544e148941"},"summary":"deploy.mjs's logged-in paths have not run: the whoami --json accounts shape, the 'already exists' patterns for r2 bucket create and queues create, artifacts namespaces list --json's shape, secret list --format json, and the account-scoped deploy with --secrets-file","supersedes":"514d6135284b54f9bfaa4bcf914f69f84183228301ae0a447aeb5f3154b2d840","tags":["deploy","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"bef595b64d34d5bcbde5cd7bd6be41ded484d86fee253b6418123a0514d03583","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":280},"end":{"line":285},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"df81d2fea0c34dd89187eef2a82e7df5abfabd2356205a8e68bf76b73e7c0193","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/smoke-remote.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"76213ba062bf2f51a9dcb6b14732a6b6df46d9fd2be975b05fdd14f2720faa03","body":{"detail":"wrangler's docs say remote: true on an artifacts binding uses the remote service in local dev; whether that holds with --local and wrangler 4.149.0 is unverified. Locally the binding answers 'Binding ARTIFACTS needs to be run remotely'. If it works it gives a probe of the real service without a deploy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":585},"end":{"line":590},"content_hash":"765d646f83c57f6bfd8c11ce9c56e0694989cbb0bd8310228dc0a9cf9e38cdfc"},"summary":"--remote-artifacts (the local Worker on the account's real Artifacts through the binding's remote: true) has not run: it needs a login, and harness.mjs starts wrangler dev with --local","supersedes":"4854d787a4833aea89d19dd5e75c7a3143dfe78c2612be02169652b1731c3277","tags":["deploy","artifacts","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:22.853436Z","id":"68b4866befebe81db5fb79f0449259300706b9edbb38a54894bab2a3f596f838","body":{"detail":"The owner is told to delete the record once set up; CLAX_TOKEN there stays valid until rotated (deploy.mjs --rotate-secrets). An alternative is printing them only and having smoke-remote.mjs take them from the environment, at the cost of the one-command smoke.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":314},"end":{"line":319},"content_hash":"414d576933fd9210f222e847e6f372f2975ebe1fa1583e8a77b8eedd6675d13d"},"summary":"deploy.mjs keeps the generated SETUP_SECRET and CLAX_TOKEN in plain text in crates/clax-worker/.deploy/<public host>.json (0600, git-ignored) so smoke-remote.mjs can use them","supersedes":"bef595b64d34d5bcbde5cd7bd6be41ded484d86fee253b6418123a0514d03583","tags":["deploy","security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364921Z","id":"98d1a8a1ce95850b42cf0ed3e0d47598f9aa65045342c8b9283e1efcf7fb7136","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-worker is its own Cargo workspace with its own lockfile (crates/clax-worker/Cargo.toml), and d223b318b added roxmltree 0.20 to crates/clax-core/Cargo.toml and the root Cargo.lock only: the Worker lock's clax-core entry lists no roxmltree and the file has no roxmltree package. A --locked build of the Worker fails, and a build without it (worker-build, crates/clax-worker/build.sh) rewrites the lock, leaving a dirty tree. 2894d3f96 fixed the same kind of drift for dirs. roxmltree 0.20 itself suits wasm32: no dependencies, #![no_std] with an std feature, #![forbid(unsafe_code)], MIT OR Apache-2.0.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":279},"end":{"line":308},"content_hash":"302203f4a7f954b6abf500cbf5502f78b50dbc66192ffdec0786279f91bdda3b"},"suggested_fix":"Add roxmltree 0.20.0 to crates/clax-worker/Cargo.lock (its checksum is in the root Cargo.lock) and to clax-core's dependency list there.","summary":"The Worker's own Cargo.lock was not updated for clax-core's new roxmltree dependency","tags":["review","icon","wasm","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
